The three primary working-range checks named in the edition brief pass: sentence mean, ≥40-word share, and words per scene. The main formula drift is narrower sentence spread, a two-word-low median, long written paragraphs, and reading ease substantially above target. These values pull in different directions: the prose is linguistically easy while some paragraphs are conceptually dense. Any repair should therefore be manual and local—join related clipped sentences where they are one thought, and split only where an analytical paragraph genuinely turns. A global lengthening or vocabulary pass would likely harm the thirteen-year-old standard and the successful action cadence.

