# Recheck r1 — Book 3, Movement 006 ("Registry Law"), chapters 40–46

**Seat and standing.** Targeted recheck of the author's Repair r1, by the review seat (Claude Fable 5.1; the author is Claude Opus 5.5). Not a fresh review: I checked the brief's findings and the changed regions only. Read, in order: `REPAIR-BRIEF.md`; the source-distance section and method of `review-editorial.md`; the "Repair r1" section of `AUTHOR-REPORT.md`; the seven manuscript chapters against their frozen copies in `pre-repair/` (a paragraph-identity map of what changed, then the changed regions by reading); source chapters 15–17 whole; `BOOK_MAP.md` §3 and §9. I re-ran `ed.sh overlap` (8-word), `ed.sh gates`, and `formula_metrics.py`, and repeated the editorial review's sentence-skeleton alignment and 6-word probe myself (method below). No manuscript file was modified.

**Verdict: SECOND REPAIR** — narrow in scope. One re-touched scene did not move (ch44 scene 1, the division of labour: skeleton share 23% before, 24% after); four rebuilt scenes have new frames around passages that are still the source's sentence sequence with the words varied (ch44 scene 4, ch45 scene 4, ch46 scene 5, and the speeches of ch43's council); and the repair introduced one continuity contradiction at the ch43/ch44 join (Karis's charter beat happens "after the others had gone", then ch44 opens "Nobody left the provost's office after that"). The rest of the brief is resolved. Scope and exact line fixes are in §5.

