## 4. Joins, referents, orphans, protected lines

**Defect — chronology at the ch43/ch44 join (introduced by the repair).** ch43 now ends with Karis catching Cael "at the foot of the worn stair after the others had gone" (the new charter beat). ch44 then opens: "Nobody left the provost's office after that; they stayed another hour with the challenge squared on the blotter and divided the three weeks up between them". The reader has just been told everyone left. ch44's breakup paragraph then has "the six of them came apart in five directions … Karis went toward the residence wing … Cael stood alone … and watched the five of them go", which contradicts Karis having lingered, and her "two steps up the passage toward the archive". Pre-repair ch43 ended on "Thank me if it works." and ch44 opened on the division; the inserted beat is in the wrong place. Fix: move Karis's beat to ch44 after the breakup paragraph, with that paragraph's Karis clause and "five directions" removed (exact strings in §5). The beat itself is good and should be kept whole.

**Slip — the aide's "All three days" (ch42) against the two-day coach (ch41).** Line fix in §5.

**Slip — "a sitting next month" (ch44, Lira).** Introduced by the re-touch (pre-repair: "a monthly sitting coming"). D6 is eight days after the council; the book teaches its reader to count. Line fix in §5.

**Wobble, inherited from the source and kept in the rebuilt scene — the digests (ch46).** Day 8: "I'm halfway through the digests." Day 10: "Then he went to the fourth shelf of the second case and brought back the enforcement digests … and he did not yet know what the record held about people like him." The second reads as a first fetch. One-word fix in §5 (optional).

**Cosmetic traces of removed scene breaks.** Two consecutive blank lines at ch42 lines 114–115 (after "I have never seen it survive.") and ch44 lines 80–81 (after "is a fight chart."). Harmless in rendering; worth tidying in the pass.

**Checked and clean.** No fragment, dangling referent or speaker separated from a line in any changed region. Every cross-reference into a rebuilt scene still has its referent: Karis's "since the scarred table on Monday night" and "On Monday, in the stable, from what you told us. *Exposes its own charter to review.*" (ch42 has Cael give them "the charter" and Coss's line is "exposes its own charter to review"); "A week ago I told a whole room I'd keep you a fighter" and "I said he would be. In the provost's office" (ch44 s1 has both); "the small box he had drawn on the night of the council" (ch44 log, Wednesday night); "the first draft in its leaning hand" (ch45); "Today proves you're real" and "The assessments that matter come later" (ch7); the Fenmark "nineteen words" (ch24, 26, 34); "A market interview … in the square" beside the Ardenmere "borrowed office" (both exist in the edition: ch6, ch13, ch39). The aide on the landing bench, then on the landing, then at the booth: consistent. The "two days in a borrowed office" / "a paper you'd found in two days": consistent.

**Protected lines (BOOK_MAP §9).** All verbatim: P15 (ch45); P17's language inside Quenna's record (ch46); "'Warden' was never a town title"; "You were fourteen." … "This is also the job."; "After that," said Quenna, "the job is to be right." (the source's own split); "New opponent. Four hundred pages, no tells, no third exchange."; Prynn's sixty-years line (words verbatim, see §3); Wray's D1 line; "Thank me if it works." P3 is echoed by Lira ("Whether you can not do it. In front of people who'd like you gone.") and not answered. Brief-quoted lines all exact except the three in §3; "I have never seen it survive." appears twice in ch42 (Coss, then Cael's retelling in italics) — fine.

**Nits, optional.** ch43 "There were six of them and five chairs, and Brom stood" — Quenna also stands (at the window, by habit), so one chair is empty; the line is good enough to keep. ch43's opening ("before the seventh bell") sits earlier in the Monday evening than ch42's close on the wall (lamps going out), and ch42's last line has him picturing the case "floor to ceiling, as deep as an old woman's arm" before ch43 shows it to him — this was in the pre-repair text, the editorial review passed the calendar, and the two readings reconcile if the notice and the archive come between supper and the wall; outside this recheck's scope. The ch41 ≥40 share stays 6.8% by design.

