**Close share 17%, ch58 at 21%.** I listed ch58's pairs at the 0.35 threshold. Of forty-odd pairs, all but four are the argument's own content, which the packet and M7 fix: the six places, "A word that isn't in the schedule isn't a classification," the four files, "If the panel decides by what's always been done, it isn't deciding by the law," the silence-as-consent exchange, "Cite the schedule entry," Ilsev's "fuller terms than you gave it yourself," the hole answer. These score close because the propositions are the same propositions; the sentences are different sentences. Four pairs are connective images that track the source: Karis's pen stopping "and then not start again … as loud as anything gets" (0.45; src "fail to start again, which in Karis was the loudest reaction available to her"); "he had said every sentence of it the way it deserved" (0.43; src "He had said every sentence the way it deserved to be said"); Ilsev "wrote a single line … and was done" (0.40); Cael at the table "with his palms on the wood" (0.44, which is also the edition's own ch47–57 habit). Judgement: ch58 is fixed content, not tracked prose; the editorial review was right to list it among the clean chapters. Fixes 4–5 recompose the two tracked images; the other two are too small to touch. The movement-wide 17% is, after that, the price of a hearing whose every proposition is canon, and is not a repair target.

