editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/manuscript/chapter-26.md:225:*The cohort has a plan. Don't chase. Make her spend. Wait for the fourth landing beat. Today it broke on one fact: you only spent two. It will not fail against somebody who makes you spend four. If you go up at the fifteenth, she will make you spend four, your whole ceiling. She's watched every burst you've taken this season and so have I.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/manuscript/chapter-22.md:1:# Chapter 22 — Minuted
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/manuscript/chapter-22.md:5:They came under the door folded in three, in a small upright hand, with the date at the top left and a subject line under it, ruled once. *Prynn's index, shelf-marks 40–60: two wrong.* *Your Lira page: she leads with the left foot on stairs. Did you know?* *Brom has my good pencil. Please recover.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/manuscript/chapter-22.md:193:Brom laughed, one short breath through the nose, and stopped, and Karis had already written it. Cael watched the words go down in her small hand, *L.: "You want it." C.: "Yes."*, with no line beneath either of them.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/manuscript/chapter-28.md:1:# Chapter 28 — Exception
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/manuscript/chapter-28.md:7:On the table in front of him lay what the afternoon had left. The warden's draft, which he had copied himself at the wing's long table not two hours since, in the round hand, every word of it, because the wing copied everything. The duty clerk's entry, four lines long: *Hall three, N. bay, 6th bell. Apparatus failure, resistance post. No evaluable content. Warden attending.* And the thing that was not on the table, because it was in him: eleven paces of open boards, and what had happened at the far end of them.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/manuscript/chapter-25.md:1:# Chapter 25 — Six and Nothing
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/manuscript/chapter-25.md:79:*Lira — Wind — Copper 2 — 6/0.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/manuscript/chapter-29.md:1:# Chapter 29 — Four Exchanges
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/manuscript/chapter-29.md:5:*One. L. spends nothing. Why?*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/manuscript/chapter-29.md:37:*Two. F. closes the doors. F. one.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/manuscript/chapter-29.md:71:*Three. L. runs the sequence and lies at four places. F.'s fourth goes into the floor. One each.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/manuscript/chapter-29.md:105:*Four. F. stops placing. L. walks in. L. two to one.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/manuscript/chapter-27.md:1:# Chapter 27 — The Pin
editions/monroe-1.3/book-04-copper-crown/manuscript/chapter-27.md:23:THE CORE MUST BE FREE BEFORE DECLARATION. CHECK THE PIN.

